WEBVTT

NOTE Narration is displayed in the caption strip below the video by default.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.794
Continue the same estimate practice guide and connected delivery map.

00:00:04.794 --> 00:00:08.630
Apply useful, clear, deliverable, responsible, sustainable and testable.

00:00:08.630 --> 00:00:14.862
Useful checks the intended action; clear checks understanding of the promise and limits.

00:00:14.862 --> 00:00:18.218
Deliverable checks material, review and support capacity.

00:00:18.218 --> 00:00:23.012
Responsible checks permission, privacy, truthful claims and the human owner.

00:00:23.012 --> 00:00:25.889
Sustainable checks continuing effort and costs.

00:00:25.889 --> 00:00:31.162
Testable checks whether a small test can answer a defined question.

00:00:31.162 --> 00:00:35.957
Keep one evidence note and one gap for each category.

00:00:35.957 --> 00:00:39.792
The earlier participation and support times remain assumptions.

00:00:39.792 --> 00:00:45.545
A polished guide or a low tool charge does not establish demand.

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:54.174
AI can organize the review, while the human identifies missing evidence and decides what is appropriate to test.

00:00:54.174 --> 00:00:57.051
Preserve the saved offer and sample.
